# EMR api requests
# Run the api with `npm run dev` inside server/ (on this machine: `env -u PORT npm run dev`, the shell exports PORT=0)
# Seed the demo data first with `npm run seed`.
# In VS Code press "Send Request" above a block. For a terminal, the curl equivalent is in the comment.

@host = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
# password for every demo account
@password = Password123!

### Health, should be 200
# curl -i http://localhost:5000/api/v1/health
GET {{host}}/health

### Sign in as super_admin, stores the cookie set by the response
# curl -i -c cookies.txt -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"email":"admin@emr.test","password":"Password123!"}' http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/login
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@emr.test",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Sign in as doctor
# @name doctorLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dr.okafor@emr.test",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Sign in as receptionist
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reception@emr.test",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Wrong password, must be a generic 401 and write a LOGIN_FAILED audit row
# curl -i -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"email":"admin@emr.test","password":"WrongPassword1!"}' http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@emr.test",
  "password": "WrongPassword1!"
}

### Unknown email, must be the same generic 401 as above
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@emr.test",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Fails validation, 400 with the field in the details
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### Who am I, paste the accessToken from a login response
# curl -i -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/me
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### No token, must be 401
GET {{host}}/auth/me

### Refresh, the browser sends the httpOnly cookie automatically
# curl -i -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/refresh
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh

### Reusing an old refresh token after a refresh, must be 401
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh

### Sign out, must be 200 even when the cookie is already gone
# curl -i -b cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/logout
POST {{host}}/auth/logout

### RBAC was proven here with a temporary GET /admin-check route (doctor 403, admin 200), which has
### been removed again. The next phase adds real role guarded routes and the checks move to those.

### The 404 shape for an unknown route
GET {{host}}/nope
